                                                </altIdentifier>
                                                <msName>Pentateuch, for Samaritan use</msName>
                                            </msIdentifier>
                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch, for Samaritan use</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="B" to="B"/>
                                                    <title>Introduction of Abū Saʿīd</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="Bv" to="67"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="67v" to="113v"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="114" to="145"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="145v" to="191"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-5-item-6">
                                                    <locus from="192" to="230"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Text identical to that of MS Arabe 3.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_41e87563292624f49dd906): 21 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 190 × 125 mm. Feuillets 8 à 19 reliés à l&apos;envers.Papier oriental.230 fol. (la foliotation compte les fol. A et B préliminaires).Écriture orientale (Égypte). Texte en partie vocalisé. Premiers mots des chapitres en hébreu, écrit en caractères samaritains.270 × 180 mm.Reliure, maroquin rouge. Armes et chiffres de Louis XV estampés à chaud.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">230 folios; the foliation includes preliminary folios A and B</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">270</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">180</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">21 lines per page. Leaves 8-19 are bound upside down.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="21" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">190</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">125</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian. Text partly vocalized. First words of chapters are in Hebrew written in Samaritan characters.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Red morocco binding with arms and ciphers of Louis XV stamped in gold.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_41e87563292624f49dd906): Pentateuque, à l&apos;usage des Samaritains. Date described in the BnF catalogue: XVe siècle.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Notices by Renaudot and J. Ascari (1735). Bought by Vansleb in Cairo; stamps with Vansleb’s cipher. Marginal glosses. Pen trials at f. A; reading mark of Buṭrus ibn Diyāb al-Ḥalabī dated 1684 at f. B; reading mark of Darwī? ibn ʿAlī dated AH 1001 / 1592-1593 at f. 230; mention of an event under the Mamlūk Qānsūḥ al-Ġūrī and a reading mark at f. 230v.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" notBefore="1401" notAfter="1500">15th century</origDate>
                                                    <p>Anonymous and undated copy.</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
